{
  "id": "20824eb1-ed54-8088-bf64-ff0ab534059e",
  "title": "Application properties and overrides",
  "sourceUrl": "https://xpandeyed.notion.site/20824eb1ed548088bf64ff0ab534059e",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-807a-a4f4-fb5724c7fdbb",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Configuration files"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-807a-a4f4-fb5724c7fdbb-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring Boot reads configuration before it creates the application beans."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-807a-a4f4-fb5724c7fdbb-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The Spring "
        ],
        [
          "Environment",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " holds the available settings and resolves their values."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-807a-a4f4-fb5724c7fdbb-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "application.properties",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " contains named settings such as "
        ],
        [
          "server.port=8081",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-807a-a4f4-fb5724c7fdbb-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "server.port",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " is a built-in setting that Spring Boot uses to configure the embedded web server."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-807a-a4f4-fb5724c7fdbb-note-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A custom setting such as "
        ],
        [
          "greeting.prefix",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " has no effect until application code reads it."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-807a-a4f4-fb5724c7fdbb-note-5",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A project normally stores its packaged settings in "
        ],
        [
          "src/main/resources/application.properties",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-807a-a4f4-fb5724c7fdbb-note-6",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "YAML is an alternative format in "
        ],
        [
          "application.yaml",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " or "
        ],
        [
          "application.yml",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "20824eb1-ed54-807a-a4f4-fb5724c7fdbb-note-7",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "If properties and YAML files exist in the same location, the properties file takes precedence."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "application-properties-lesson-1",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Overrides"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "application-properties-lesson-1-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring Boot can read the same setting from a file, an environment variable, a JVM system property, or an application argument."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "application-properties-lesson-1-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The source with higher precedence supplies the value when several sources define the same key."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "application-properties-lesson-1-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The table shows the order for these common sources. Spring Boot supports additional sources."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "application-properties-lesson-1-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A packaged file travels inside the JAR. An external configuration file can supply different values for a run."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "application-properties-lesson-1-note-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "By default, Spring Boot also looks in the working directory, its "
        ],
        [
          "config/",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " directory, and immediate child directories of "
        ],
        [
          "config/",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          "."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "application-properties-lesson-1-note-5",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "External files override packaged files in the normal configuration search."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "application-properties-lesson-1-note-6",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Credentials belong in a secret source rather than a committed configuration file."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "application-properties-lesson-1-example-0",
      "type": "example",
      "example": {
        "title": "Set and override the server port",
        "language": "text",
        "description": [
          "Each example is a separate project. All required application files appear in the tabs.",
          "The commands run from the directory containing `pom.xml` in a Unix shell.",
          "The packaged JAR is `target/demo.jar`. The command-line property selects port `9091`."
        ],
        "code": "",
        "explanation": [
          "The file supplies `8081` as the port when no higher-priority source sets it.",
          "`SERVER_PORT` is the environment-variable form of `server.port`.",
          "The application argument selects `9091`, so this run listens on port `9091`.",
          "`spring.application.name` names the application. It does not change an endpoint path.",
          "`greeting.prefix` is available to application code. Reading it is covered in Read configuration in Java."
        ],
        "commands": "mvn package -DskipTests\nSERVER_PORT=9090 java -jar target/demo.jar --server.port=9091",
        "files": [
          {
            "name": "src/main/resources/application.properties",
            "language": "text",
            "code": "server.port=8081\nspring.application.name=greeting-app\ngreeting.prefix=Hello\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/GreetingController.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\nimport org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.GetMapping;\nimport org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RestController;\n@RestController\npublic class GreetingController {\n    @GetMapping(\"/greetings\")\n    public String greet() { return \"Hello, Ada\"; }\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "pom.xml",
            "language": "text",
            "code": "<project xmlns=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\"\n         xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd\">\n    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>\n    <parent>\n        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>\n        <version>3.5.16</version>\n        <relativePath/>\n    </parent>\n    <groupId>com.example</groupId>\n    <artifactId>demo</artifactId>\n    <version>1.0.0</version>\n    <properties><java.version>17</java.version></properties>\n    <dependencies>\n        <dependency>\n            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>\n        </dependency>\n    </dependencies>\n    <build>\n        <finalName>demo</finalName>\n        <plugins>\n            <plugin>\n                <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n                <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>\n            </plugin>\n        </plugins>\n    </build>\n\n</project>\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/DemoApplication.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;\nimport org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;\n\n@SpringBootApplication\npublic class DemoApplication {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        SpringApplication.run(DemoApplication.class, args);\n    }\n}\n"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
